continuing on the sentencing phase just  wrapped up for the day for the box truck  driver who killed five  cyclists in december right near  searchlight 45 year old jordan varsity  admitted he was  under the influence of methamphetamine  when he ran  into a group of cyclists on u.s 95 joe  mohler was in the courtroom where  relatives of victims shared their  struggles without their loved ones  brian it was an emotional day in court  today we heard of from some of the  family of the victims and the accused  jordan barson  back in april barson entered a plea  agreement reducing the number of charges  he was facing to two counts of dui  resulting in death  family of some of the victims described  how the sudden deaths of their loved  ones changed their lives  douglas murray the brother of michael  murray looked at barson expressing his  loss  you can also see farson's reaction  jordan barson  there are no words there are no words  to express what you've done to our  family  what you did to my brother i can't  imagine him laying out there in the  road looking at the carnage  that this man created  at the start of the sentencing hearing  barson stood up via video and said he  was sorry and that  he was ashamed with himself he says  after he gets out of prison he wants to  share his  story at rehab facilities prevent  another tragedy like this now barson  faces up to 40 years  in jail we will hear from more family  members when the sentencing continues  tomorrow reporting live outside the  courthouse jill mullen 8 news now
 

